IMPORT prelude

-- National Registration Act 1965 (Singapore) -- who must register, names, identity cards, change of
-- residence and the contact address, householders' returns, cancellation, and proof: ss 2, 3 and 5 to 15
-- and the Schedule.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/NRA1965.txt (incorporating Act 16 of 2026, the Cross-Border Railways
-- amendments in force 30 September 2026). The deposit's arrangement of sections runs one ahead of the body;
-- the encoding follows the body.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. 37 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository name it, and 21 of those cite s 10,
-- the change-of-address report: other Acts deem a person to have told them of a move if the person reports it
-- under s 10 (see s 11).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage
-- table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md. No regulations under s 33 were retrieved,
-- and the exemptions from registration live there.

§ `National Registration Act 1965 -- registration`

§§ `2(3) and the Schedule -- personal identifiers`

-- Schedule: "1. A person's fingerprint or handprint ... 2. A photograph or other image of a person's face and
-- shoulders. 3. An image of a person's iris ... 4. A person's signature."
-- s 2(3): the Minister may amend the Schedule by order, but any other identifier "(a) must be an image, a
-- measurement or a recording of an EXTERNAL part of the human body, or a measurement or a recording of a person's
-- VOICE; and (b) must not be an identifier the obtaining of which would involve the taking of an INVASIVE SAMPLE".
DECLARE Identifier IS ONE OF
    `a fingerprint`
    `a facial photograph`
    `an iris image`
    `a signature`
    `a voice recording`
    `a gait measurement`
    `a DNA sample from a cheek swab`
    `a blood sample`

GIVEN `the identifier` IS AN Identifier
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the identifier is in the Schedule now` IF
    CONSIDER `the identifier`
    WHEN `a fingerprint` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a facial photograph` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an iris image` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a signature` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Whether a cheek swab is "invasive" is fixed by s 8 of the Registration of Criminals Act 1949, which this row does
-- not read; the encoding assumes any DNA or blood sample is internal material and so outside (a) either way.
GIVEN `the identifier` IS AN Identifier
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may add the identifier by order` IF
    CONSIDER `the identifier`
    WHEN `a voice recording` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a gait measurement` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a DNA sample from a cheek swab` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a blood sample` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `3(4), (5) -- who may be a registration officer`

-- s 3(4): the Commissioner may appoint as a registration officer (a) a public officer, (b) an employee of a public
-- authority, or (c) an employee of a prescribed institution. s 3(5): "only a PUBLIC OFFICER may be appointed as a
-- registration officer for the purposes of section 21, 22, 24 or 25" -- the demand to surrender, arrest and search,
-- investigation, and notices to attend court.
DECLARE Appointee IS ONE OF
    `a public officer`
    `an employee of a public authority`
    `an employee of a prescribed institution`
    `a private contractor`

DECLARE Purpose IS ONE OF
    `registration and issuing cards`
    `demanding surrender of a suspicious card`
    `arrest, search and detention`
    `investigation`
    `notices to attend court`

GIVEN `the appointee` IS AN Appointee, `the purpose` IS A Purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may be appointed a registration officer for the purpose` IF
    CONSIDER `the appointee`
    WHEN `a private contractor` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a public officer` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `the purpose`
        WHEN `registration and issuing cards` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `6, 9 -- who must register`

-- s 6: "Subject to section 7 and any exemptions which may be granted by regulations made under section 33, every
-- person LAWFULLY RESIDENT within Singapore must be registered". s 9: every person registered "must be issued with an
-- identity card".
--
-- The Act does not confine registration to citizens and permanent residents. Anyone lawfully resident must register
-- unless the regulations exempt them; this row has not retrieved the regulations.
GIVEN `lawfully resident in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `exempted by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person must be registered` IF
    `lawfully resident in Singapore` AND NOT `exempted by regulations`

§§ `7 -- the 1990 re-registration`

-- s 7(1), (2): cards issued before 3 June 1990 ceased to be valid on the expiry of the re-registration period the
-- Minister gazetted. s 7(3): a late re-registration is still possible. Dates as yyyymmdd.
GIVEN `issued on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the card is a pre-1990 card that has ceased to be valid` IF
    `issued on` LESS THAN 19900603

§§ `8 -- names`

-- s 8(1): a name entered or altered "(a) must be in a form expressed in characters in the modern English alphabet;
-- (b) may include a permitted character; and (c) must not exceed the number of characters permitted in the electronic
-- form of the register".
-- s 8(2): the Commissioner MAY refuse a name that "(a) contains anything that represents or resembles a title, a rank
-- or an award; (b) where the name adopts a patronymic or matronymic naming system ..., includes any expression or
-- abbreviation ... that does not correspond to the person's sex ...; (c) is obscene or offensive; or (d) is contrary to
-- the public interest."
--
-- The s 8(1) conditions are mandatory; the s 8(2) grounds are discretionary. A name in Chinese characters cannot be
-- entered at all (s 8(1)(a)) unless the characters are "permitted characters" under the Registration of Births and
-- Deaths Act 2021, which this row does not read.
DECLARE ProposedName HAS
    `in modern English alphabet characters, or permitted characters` IS A BOOLEAN
    `within the register's character limit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `resembles a title, rank or award` IS A BOOLEAN
    `uses bin, binti, s/o, d/o or similar not matching the person's sex` IS A BOOLEAN
    `obscene or offensive` IS A BOOLEAN
    `contrary to the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the name` IS A ProposedName
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the name meets section 8(1)` IF
        `the name`'s `in modern English alphabet characters, or permitted characters`
    AND `the name`'s `within the register's character limit`

GIVEN `the name` IS A ProposedName
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commissioner may refuse the name` IF
        NOT `the name meets section 8(1)` `the name`
    OR  `the name`'s `resembles a title, rank or award`
    OR  `the name`'s `uses bin, binti, s/o, d/o or similar not matching the person's sex`
    OR  `the name`'s `obscene or offensive`
    OR  `the name`'s `contrary to the public interest`

GIVEN `the name` IS A ProposedName
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commissioner must refuse the name` IF
    NOT `the name meets section 8(1)` `the name`

§§ `10 -- change of residence, and the contact address`

-- s 10(1): a registered person who changes residence "must, within 28 DAYS thereof, report the change".
-- s 10(2): a person who moves OUTSIDE Singapore "may inform a registration officer of his or her contact address in
-- Singapore, which must be -- (a) the address of any premises in Singapore which he or she still owns an estate or
-- interest in and which is used or permitted under written law to be used as residence; or (b) the address of the place
-- of residence in Singapore of -- (i) his or her spouse, grandparent, parent, sibling, child or grandchild; (ii) any
-- grandparent, parent or sibling of his or her spouse; or (iii) any sibling of any of his or her parents or his or her
-- spouse's parents or any child of any of his or her siblings or spouse's siblings."
-- s 16(1)(c): informing a registration officer of a contact address "that is false or is not an address described in
-- section 10(2)(a) or (b)" is an offence -- $5,000 or 5 years.
--
-- The list reaches aunts and uncles, nephews and nieces, and the spouse's, but not COUSINS, not step-relations, not
-- in-laws beyond the spouse's grandparents, parents and siblings, and not friends. A Singaporean abroad who gives a
-- cousin's or a best friend's flat commits an offence carrying up to five years.
DECLARE Relation IS ONE OF
    `spouse`
    `grandparent`
    `parent`
    `sibling`
    `child`
    `grandchild`
    `spouse's grandparent`
    `spouse's parent`
    `spouse's sibling`
    `aunt or uncle`
    `spouse's aunt or uncle`
    `nephew or niece`
    `spouse's nephew or niece`
    `cousin`
    `step-parent`
    `sibling's spouse`
    `friend`

GIVEN `the relation` IS A Relation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the relative's residence may be the contact address` IF
    CONSIDER `the relation`
    WHEN `cousin` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `step-parent` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `sibling's spouse` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `friend` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE ContactAddress HAS
    `the person has moved outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `premises the person still has an estate or interest in, usable as a residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the residence of a relative` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the relation` IS A Relation
    `the address is true` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the address` IS A ContactAddress
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contact address is a permitted one` IF
        `the address`'s `the address is true`
    AND (    `the address`'s `premises the person still has an estate or interest in, usable as a residence`
         OR  (    `the address`'s `the residence of a relative`
              AND `the relative's residence may be the contact address` (`the address`'s `the relation`)))

GIVEN `the address` IS A ContactAddress
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `giving the contact address is an offence` IF
    NOT `the contact address is a permitted one` `the address`

GIVEN `days since moving` IS A NUMBER, `reported` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is in breach of the 28-day duty` IF
        `days since moving` GREATER THAN 28
    AND NOT `reported`

§§ `11 -- passing on the change of address`

-- s 11(1): where another written law both requires a person to tell a department of a move AND deems a s 10 report to be
-- compliance, the Commissioner must transmit the change on the person's s 10 report.
-- s 11(2): "(a) neither the Government nor any registration officer nor any authorised person ... shall be liable for any
-- loss or damage ... as a result of any error or omission ... IF such error or omission was made in GOOD FAITH and in
-- the ordinary course of the discharge of the duties ...; and (b) the Government department ... to which ... the
-- information has been transmitted shall not be liable for any loss or damage ... as a result of any error or omission
-- ... HOWEVER CAUSED by any registration officer or authorised person".
--
-- The transmitter's immunity needs good faith. The recipient department's does not: it is immune for an error "however
-- caused", even one made in bad faith by the transmitting officer.
DECLARE TransmissionFacts HAS
    `the other law requires the person to report a move to the department` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other law deems a section 10 report to be compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person made a section 10 report` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A TransmissionFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commissioner must transmit the change` IF
        `the facts`'s `the other law requires the person to report a move to the department`
    AND `the facts`'s `the other law deems a section 10 report to be compliance`
    AND `the facts`'s `the person made a section 10 report`

DECLARE Defendant IS ONE OF
    `the Government or the transmitting officer`
    `the receiving department`

GIVEN `the defendant` IS A Defendant, `the error was made in good faith in the ordinary course of duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the defendant is immune from liability for the transmission error` IF
    CONSIDER `the defendant`
    WHEN `the Government or the transmitting officer` THEN `the error was made in good faith in the ordinary course of duty`
    WHEN `the receiving department` THEN TRUE

§§ `12 -- householders' returns`

-- s 12(1): every householder ("the owner, tenant, subtenant or occupier of a house, shophouse, flat, apartment, hut or
-- other dwelling place", s 2(1)) must, "when so required in writing by a registration officer", submit returns.
-- s 16(1)(d): failing to submit, or to submit in time, is an offence -- $5,000 or 5 years.
GIVEN `is a householder` IS A BOOLEAN, `required in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `submitted in time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the householder commits the returns offence` IF
    `is a householder` AND `required in writing` AND NOT `submitted in time`

§§ `13 -- cancellation`

-- s 13(1): the Minister may order cancellation where satisfied the registration "(a) was obtained by means of fraud,
-- false representation or the concealment of any material fact; or (b) was effected by MISTAKE".
-- s 13(2): the person "must forthwith surrender his or her identity card"; failing to is an offence under s 16(1)(g),
-- $5,000 or 5 years. No appeal is provided.
--
-- Limb (b) does not ask whose mistake. A registration effected by the Registry's own error may be cancelled, and the
-- person who did nothing wrong then commits a five-year offence by not surrendering the card at once.
DECLARE CancellationGround IS ONE OF
    `fraud, false representation or concealment of a material fact`
    `a mistake by the applicant`
    `a mistake by the registration officer`
    `the Minister's dislike of the person`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A CancellationGround
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may order the registration cancelled` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `the Minister's dislike of the person` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act provides an appeal against cancellation` IF
    FALSE

§§ `14, 15 -- proof`

-- s 14: "The onus of proving the truth of the contents of any written application for registration ... or the contents
-- of an identity card is on the applicant or on the person to whom the identity card was issued or on ANY OTHER PERSON
-- ALLEGING the truth of the contents."
-- s 15(1): a claim to citizenship by birth may not be accepted unless the person produces "a birth certificate or other
-- evidence to the registration officer's satisfaction"; (2) the onus is on the claimant; (3) a birth certificate without
-- the child's name, even with a statutory declaration, or an old identity card stating birth in Singapore, "is not
-- necessarily sufficient evidence".
--
-- s 14 means an identity card is not evidence of its own contents against the State: the holder must prove them.
DECLARE BirthEvidence IS ONE OF
    `a birth certificate naming the person`
    `a birth certificate without the child's name`
    `an unnamed birth certificate with a statutory declaration`
    `a 1955 Ordinance identity card stating birth in Singapore`
    `nothing`

GIVEN `the evidence` IS A BirthEvidence, `the officer is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim to citizenship by birth may be accepted` IF
    CONSIDER `the evidence`
    WHEN `nothing` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE `the officer is satisfied`

GIVEN `the evidence` IS A BirthEvidence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the evidence is necessarily sufficient` IF
    FALSE

DECLARE Party IS ONE OF
    `the applicant or card holder`
    `another person alleging the contents are true`
    `the Commissioner alleging the contents are false`

GIVEN `the party` IS A Party
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the party bears the onus of proving the contents true` IF
    CONSIDER `the party`
    WHEN `the Commissioner alleging the contents are false` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE
